---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---
<Base title="Colophon" description="How this site is built, and the decisions behind it.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="label"><b>Colophon</b> / How it’s made</p>
    <h1>How this site <em class="hl">works</em>.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Same format as the rest of the site: what I picked, and what it cost.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose cv">
    <h2>Static pages</h2>
    <p>
      Every post and every DSA note is its own plain HTML page, built with
      Astro. Search engines and people with JavaScript off get the same page as
      everyone else. The catch is that publishing means rebuilding. That takes
      about three seconds, so I’ll live.
    </p>

    <h2>Notes from the vault</h2>
    <p>
      The DSA notes live in my Obsidian vault, and the build reads them
      straight from there. Wikilinks turn into real links, Obsidian-only
      blocks get dropped. I never copy a note into this repo, which also means
      the site can’t build without the vault sitting next to it.
    </p>

    <h2>The look</h2>
    <p>
      A sheet of paper with hairlines: rails down both sides, square cells that share their borders, and little crosses where the lines meet. I lifted that from <a href="https://getartcraft.com/apps">ArtCraft</a>.
      The teal and the ledge under every button come from my own apps, <a href="https://github.com/Navknight/rituals">Rituals</a> and <a href="https://github.com/Navknight/tally">Tally</a>.
      Text is Archivo, stretched wide for headings. Labels, diagrams and code are in <a href="https://commitmono.com">Commit Mono</a>.
      The diagrams are hand-placed SVG, so moving a box means editing coordinates. Worth it.
    </p>

    <h2>Very little JavaScript</h2>
    <p>
      Scripts handle the theme switch, search, the clock in the corner, the
      problem filter and the lab games. Nothing fades in as you scroll, and
      there’s one stylesheet and no framework.
    </p>

    <h2>No tracking</h2>
    <p>
      There are no analytics or cookies. The only thing stored is your light or
      dark choice, in your own browser. I have no idea if you’re reading this, which
      is honestly a bit freeing.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      GitHub Pages. The source is on <a href="https://github.com/Navknight/navknight.github.io">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
